## DESCRIPTION
## Calculus Two, Sequences
## ENDDESCRIPTION

## DBsubject(Calculus - single variable)
## DBchapter(Infinite sequences and series)
## DBsection(Limit of a sequence)
## Date(09/16/2018)
## Institution(Community College of Denver, Colorado Community College System)
## Author(Brittni Lorton)
## KEYWORDS('calculus', 'sequences', 'limit of a sequence')

DOCUMENT();

loadMacros("PGstandard.pl", "PGML.pl", "PGcourse.pl",);

Context('Numeric')->variables->are(n => "Real");

$a = random(2, 5);
$b = random(2, 5);
$c = random(2, 5);

BEGIN_PGML

Find the limit of the sequence [``\{a_n\} = \left\{\ln\left(\frac{n+[$a]}{[$b]n^2-[$c]}\right)\right\}``].


[``\lim_{n \to \infty} a_n=``][_]{Compute("-inf")}

END_PGML

BEGIN_PGML_SOLUTION
[``` \begin{aligned}
\lim_{n \to \infty} a_n & = \lim_{n \to \infty} \ln\left(\frac{n+[$a]}{[$b]n^2-[$c]}\right) \\
& = \ln\left(\lim_{n \to \infty} \frac{n+[$a]}{[$b]n^2-[$c]}\right)
\end{aligned}```]
Because 
[```\lim_{n \to \infty} \frac{n+[$a]}{[$b]n^2-[$c]}  = 0```]
and 
[``` \lim_{x \to 0^+} \ln x = -\infty, ```] then the limit of the sequence is [`-\infty`].
END_PGML_SOLUTION

ENDDOCUMENT();
